+## Durable capture records
+
+`records` stores a completed `workspace::Capture` and reads its exact bytes and
+provenance back later, including after the originating files and Git objects are
+gone. The store is a local SQLite database; the interface is library-only.
+
+```rust,no_run
+use anti_slop::{
+    records::{Budget, Store},
+    workspace::{CaptureRequest, Selection, capture},
+};
+use std::path::Path;
+
+let captured = capture(
+    Path::new("/path/to/repository"),
+    &CaptureRequest::new(Selection::Local),
+)?;
+let mut store = Store::open_with_budget(
+    Path::new("/workspace/.anti-slop/records.sqlite3"),
+    Budget::default(), // 10 GiB per workspace
+)?;
+let saved = store.save_capture(&captured)?;
+let retained = store.read_capture(saved.id)?;
+# Ok::<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>(())
+```
+
+A save retains the source bytes, roles, generations, Git blob and mode
+identities, comparison selection/commit, configuration identity and bytes in
+one SQLite transaction. A returned `SavedCapture` follows a completed commit and
+carries the measured retained footprint. Reads verify a records-owned integrity
+digest over the complete membership, provenance and bytes; missing, altered,
+duplicate or extra evidence returns an explicit corruption error. Retained reads
+include deletion-versus-empty distinctions, valid empty captures and independent
+occurrences of equal content.
+
+WAL mode with `synchronous = FULL` provides the selected durability; SQLite
+removes the WAL when the last connection closes. The store enforces an
+application admission budget (10 GiB default, warning at 80%, explicit refusal
+at the limit). The reservation covers database pages, WAL/SHM/journal files,
+checkpoint duplication and the existing WAL backlog; it is an engineering
+allowance under the bundled SQLite settings, not a hard filesystem quota.
+Opening a store below its retained size does not prevent retained reads.
+
+The store uses schema version 1, which has not shipped; no migration history is
+provided. Purge/export, analysis, report rendering and admission for model work
+are later outcomes. `cargo test --frozen --test records` exercises the public
+library boundary; the record code has no analysis or CLI command.
+
 ## Toolchain and dependencies
 
 - One Cargo package: `anti-slop`; library: `anti_slop`; binary: `anti-slop`.
